note S5 scrub and a global declared after a function that scrubs: that function is compiled before the
note global exists, so the global must not take a pinned register its scrub would clear and not restore
note (omc 0d7f2f42 pinned it: the in-range read after the call trapped 3, exit 103). Exit 0 is the pass.
om2
fn clean to ulong
k = scrub 64
ret ulong k
end
global g ulong 5000
fn main to int
j = ulong 4999
put g j 7
k = clean
y = get g j
if ne y 7
ret 2
end
ret int k
end
